From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:15:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: pm8226: estimate charge from real OCV and coulombs

Use a held hardware snapshot of BMS1 OCV, signed 36-bit main coulomb
counter and average sense voltage. Always restore the previous hold bit,
including failed reads. Apply the sibling IADC's measured gain correction
and the board's sense resistance. Track counter wrap in software without
clearing or reconfiguring the BMS or charger.

Add the original Samsung 6800 mAh cell OCV tables with their GPL-2.0-only
license and copyright. Use power_supply_battery_info to convert measured
OCV to an initial charge, subtract the measured discharge coulombs and
report charge_now, capacity and signed current_now through the normal ABI.

The physical SM-T531's saved cpuinfo reports Revision0003. The exact
MACH_MATISSE3G_OPEN BSP selects 12200 micro-ohms above revision2. Its old
installed Android ROM used an inferred12500 micro-ohms; the2.4% difference
remains a documented model/calibration uncertainty pending measurement.
The model does not learn cell ageing or usable charge under load; it must
be validated on real discharge/recharge and cold boot before production.

Register/conversion reference: Samsung MSM8226 BSP
3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256, drivers/power/qpnp-bms.c.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
